3. CONDITIONALS (`if/elif/else`), LOOPS & COMPREHENSIONS
================================================================================
Conditionals control business rules (like KDS timer colors and loyalty reward unlocks), while loops and list comprehensions process menus and bills in one clean line.

A. KDS Urgency Timer Logic (`if / elif / else`):
```python
def get_kds_card_color(elapsed_minutes: int) -> str:
    if elapsed_minutes <= 5:
        return "GREEN"    # New order
    elif elapsed_minutes <= 12:
        return "YELLOW"   # Cooking long
    else:
        return "RED"      # Late / Overdue

print(get_kds_card_color(3))   # GREEN
print(get_kds_card_color(9))   # YELLOW
print(get_kds_card_color(15))  # RED
```

B. Loops & List Comprehensions (Filtering & Bill Sum):
```python
# Filter only Veg items using a list comprehension
veg_items = [item for item in cart_items if item["is_veg"] is True]

# Route items to the Tandoor station
tandoor_orders = [item["name"] for item in cart_items if item["station"] == "Tandoor"]

# Calculate cart subtotal using sum()
subtotal = sum(item["qty"] * item["price"] for item in cart_items)
print(f"Subtotal: Rs.{subtotal:.2f}")
```

