5. OBJECT-ORIENTED PROGRAMMING (OOP) FOR MODELS & SCHEMAS
================================================================================
SQLAlchemy database tables and Pydantic schemas are both Python classes. Understanding `__init__`, attributes, methods, and inheritance makes backend coding effortless.

```python
class MenuItem:
    def __init__(self, item_id: int, name: str, price_full: float, station: str, is_veg: bool = True):
        self.item_id = item_id
        self.name = name
        self.price_full = price_full
        self.station = station
        self.is_veg = is_veg

    def apply_discount(self, discount_percent: float) -> float:
        discounted = self.price_full * (1 - discount_percent / 100)
        return round(discounted, 2)

# Inheritance: DealItem inherits everything from MenuItem
class DealItem(MenuItem):
    def __init__(self, item_id: int, name: str, price_full: float, station: str, badge: str):
        super().__init__(item_id, name, price_full, station)
        self.badge = badge

paneer = DealItem(1, "Paneer Tikka Platter", 300.0, "Tandoor", "Deal of the Day")
print(f"{paneer.name} [{paneer.badge}] -> Deal Price: Rs.{paneer.apply_discount(15)}")
```

